{"seq":22,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/claude-code-opus-no-identity-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:56:28.806Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"2ba98af5f9b0ca7b2221d66bbad58fd9b973f618972278fc7327c5a4b239acf4","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes I could find. They're the digests in the shared team folders; there's nothing under a members/moss notes folder. Two ticket numbers are for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift went through without problems. The same note also has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other North digests (9/14/2025 pipeline, 3/23/2026 renewal) mention QFL but don't give any ticket numbers. The Central digests mention tickets #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are for Marrow accounts, not QFL."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
